{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112764","id":3011135160,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6zeka4","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112764","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112764.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112764.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112764","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112764/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112764/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112764/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7bcda31d0f575796e39500514a162b4f1bb717d4","number":112764,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Clean up argument passing for export callbacks","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`EditorExportSaveFunction`, as exposed by `EditorExportPlatform`, has slowly grown to accept more and more arguments, to the point of being unwieldy. Not only that, but since `EditorExportSaveFunction` is implemented all over the place you also end up with a lot of boilerplate whenever you do want to add anything new to `EditorExportSaveFunction`.\r\n\r\nThis pull request tries to resolve this by doing the following:\r\n\r\n1. Introduce a new `EditorExportPlatform::SaveFileInfo` struct meant to hold anything that isn't the file data itself. This is similar to what's found in #87696.\r\n2. Change the expected callback signature of `save_cb` in `EditorExportPlatform.export_project_files` to instead take the equivalent of `SaveFileInfo` as a `Dictionary`.\r\n3. Stop passing encryption data through the export callbacks and instead fetch it through `EditorExportPreset`.\r\n4. Added and bound a new `resolve_encryption_key` method to `EditorExportPreset`, which will convert either the preset key or the `GODOT_SCRIPT_ENCRYPTION_KEY` environment variable to a `PackedByteArray`. This is necessary since we no longer pass the binary encryption key to `save_cb`. I'm open to renaming this though.\r\n\r\nI also took the liberty of including the following (mostly unrelated) changes:\r\n\r\n1. Added a new `source_path` property to `EditorExportPlatform::SaveFileInfo`, to represent the source path, as opposed to the exported/remapped path. This will allow for things like #113240.\r\n2. Renamed `EditorExportSaveFunction`, `EditorExportRemoveFunction` and `EditorExportSaveSharedObject` to `SaveFileFunction`, `RemoveFileFunction` and `SaveSharedObjectFunction` respectively, since the prefix seemed redundant given the type nesting.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2909900850,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyOTA5OTAwODUw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:export","name":"topic:expor